    "title": "Average delay",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-02T14:06:20Z",
    "description": "<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"4731\">For the given set of filter data (i.e. date range, granularity (hour, day, or month), operator and line), the query will return:</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"4861\"><strong>scheduled_departures:</strong> total number of scheduled stop departures in the filter set</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"4944\"><strong>total_departures:</strong> total number of actual stop departures observed</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"5011\"><strong>total_delay:</strong> sum of differences between actual and scheduled departure times (in seconds).</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"5103\">So then we can formulate the average delay = <strong>total_delay / total_departures</strong></p>",
    "description_text": " For the given set of filter data (i.e. date range, granularity (hour, day, or month), operator and line), the query will return:  scheduled_departures: total number of scheduled stop departures in the filter set  total_departures: total number of actual stop departures observed  total_delay: sum of differences between actual and scheduled departure times (in seconds).  So then we can formulate the average delay = total_delay / total_departures ",
